    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. You mentioned the concerns are \"highly valid\" because of recent court scrutiny, but some of the opponents argue that the changes are necessary specifically to maintain public confidence in election integrity and to prevent potential fraud. Is there a way to look at those integrity concerns as being just as legitimate as the concerns about voter access?",
